# BARBELL ROW

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Barbell Row is a bilateral upper-body compound exercise designed to develop horizontal pulling strength through coordinated shoulder extension, scapular retraction and trunk stabilization.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the foundational exercises for developing posterior-chain integration, pulling strength and postural robustness.

---

# Philosophy

Strong athletes do not only push.

They must also pull.

The Barbell Row develops the ability to generate force while maintaining trunk stability under load.

CAS selects this exercise when horizontal pulling strength provides meaningful transfer to combat performance.

