# Scientific Evidence

Evidence Level

★★★★★

The Barbell Row is strongly supported for improving upper-body pulling strength, posterior-chain integration and scapular function. It complements vertical pulling exercises by developing horizontal force production and trunk stability.

---

# Explainability

Example

The Barbell Row is selected because combat athletes frequently generate force while maintaining a strong forward posture.

Improving horizontal pulling strength enhances clinch control, posture breaking, grip fighting and upper-body robustness.

